PRETABLE_7 -- pvrrenderexit, test-variant table 7 (repair 7; the ruling's PRETABLE_8, numbered here by repair; 164 rows).
Written BEFORE meas7b and BEFORE table 7: its mtime must precede every result in meas7b/ and table7/ (the frozen probe is
copied first and is older).  INSTRUMENT: table7/probe164_frozen.py, cmp-identical to cand164_probe.py (the shipped 148 rows plus
the 16 repair-7 rows; base164/: 164/164 on build/, both clearance parts recorded; head164/: 78/164 pre-fix).
INSTRUMENT_MD5 ebce4d7f4c91c837f64232ea03150dbd table7/probe164_frozen.py
Baseline: dev_pvr.c.fix7 (== GXEMUL-SEC src/devices/dev_pvr.c).  Variants: pvr_table7.py -- table 5's 190 and the 16 cells.
EVERY prediction is EXACT -- the full red set, none = all 164 green -- except Y2s/Y2t/Y4s/Y4t (undefined behaviour, NOT
PREDICTED).  148 carried rows: MEASURED (table 5; meas7 for FB1s FB2s FB1t FB2t PC1t; the eleven new cells green there, each
register being 0 = the constant).  16 new rows: DERIVED -- per cell (CELL7), and for table 5's 190 by geometry (NEWMAP:
each edge row repeats an existing row's geometry, rasterizer and Z-state at another frame base or rows) plus FBHI_RED.
ONE per-row exception: Nt_inner_or is predicted on 160 rows and NOT PREDICTED on the four palcfg rows (undefined behaviour,
CHANNELS7 below).
206 variants: 202 predicted, 172 predicted red, 30 predicted green (table 5's 30, reasons carried), 4 NOT PREDICTED.
Legs: base 164/164; HEAD 78/164 SYMPTOM=PRESENT (MEASURED already, head164/); null media CONTROL=FAIL: /bin/true 9/164, an
absent binary 0/164, /bin/false 1/164.

GUARD FIELD vs BODY FIELD (the pre-table check, as the ruling's section 2 states it):
  simpleline -- guard operands of P1-P3 and P7: y, x1, x2, x, d->ysize, d->xsize and the constant 0 (`y < 0`, `x1 < 0`, `x2 < 0`
    at dev_pvr.c:658; `x > 0` at :684).  Body-read lvalues: d->vram_z[ofs], z, d->zwrite_disabled, r g b, d->bytes_per_pixel,
    d->vram[fbofs], and d->reg through ONE spelling: fb_base = REG(PVRREG_FB_RENDER_ADDR1) (:662, read :715).
  texturedline -- the same guard operands at :731 and :769.  Body-read lvalues: as simpleline, and d->reg through THREE
    spellings: fb_base (:735, read :775); palette_cfg = d->reg[PVRREG_PALETTE_CFG / 4] & PVR_PALETTE_CFG_MODE_MASK (:760, read
    :845); d->reg[PVRREG_PALETTE / 4], read directly as the palette base (:842).  The texture parameters are the caller's reads
    (:1047), outside the boundary; ofs, fbofs, bytesperpixel and the slopes are derived inputs, graded by the body's tests on them.
  Partitions the body induces: fb_base -- none, used only in arithmetic (:715, :775); SAMPLED at 0 (every carried session),
    0x200000 (fbhi) and 0x300000 (fbedge, fbtedge).  palette_cfg -- {0, 1, 2, 3} by the switch at :845-868, reached only for pixel
    format 6, which no session renders: SAMPLED at 0 and 3 at the guard; the switch partition is clause-(e) DEBT, disclosed.
    PALETTE[0] -- none, a palette entry (data): SAMPLED at 0 and 0x10000.
  Disagreeing state owed: each register non-zero, which no carried session sets (DEVINIT zeroes d->reg; the probe never wrote
    them) -- the eight repair-7 sessions.  (The ruling places `x2 < 0` at :659 / :732; it is on :658 / :731, with `x1 < 0`.)

STEP 2 (meas7b, before the rows ship): the eleven unmeasured cells -- FB3s FB4s FB3t FB4t PC2t PC3t PC4t PL1t PL2t PL3t PL4t --
  on probe148_frozen.py: 148/148 each; on table7/probe164_frozen.py: exactly the sets their VARIANTS lines below give
  (pvr_table7.py check7b).

CHANNELS of the 16 repair-7 rows (pixel, want; the variants that move each and the observable -- DERIVED from dev_pvr.c):
  fbhi s px (120,105) RED, frame 0x200000 -- FBA (Z-on, simpleline) row 105 spans 105..135.  Red: FB1s (`x > fb_base`: no column),
    FB2s (`y < fb_base`: every row returns) -- black.  Table 5: none; the all-Z-on lone interior `ovon t1 only` is green under all 190.
  fbhi t px (220,105) RED -- FBB (Z-on, textured, u = v = 0, texel (0,0) red) row 105 spans 205..235.  Red: FB1t, FB2t.  Table 5:
    none (`texbeh t1 only` reds only under B1_exit, for the Z-off header this session does not have).
  zfbhi s px, zfbhi t px -- the Z-off twins: the same cells, plus B1_exit (the session ends), M11 (the Z-off polygon declined), M12 (s)
    and M28 (t) (the Z-off span not drawn) -- exactly the variants that red `ovoff t1 only` / `texoff t1 only` in table 5.
  fbedge l tip (1,259) RED, frame 0x300000 -- LREV row 259 arrives 1.0 / -1.0 and is swapped: column 1.  Red: FB1s, FB2s, FB3s
    (`x1 < fb_base && x2 < 0` returns the row).  Table 5: as `edges2 l tip` -- the same triangle, rasterizer and Z state, nothing else
    drawn reaches row 259, and no table-5 variant reads fb_base, fbofs or the frame check.
  fbedge x2 tip (1,159) RED -- LEFT3 row 159 spans -1.0..1.0: column 1.  Red: FB1s, FB2s, FB4s (`x1 < 0 && x2 < fb_base` returns it).
    Table 5: as `edges2 x2 tip`.
  zfbedge l tip, zfbedge x2 tip -- the Z-off twins: the same cells; table 5 as `zedges2 l tip` and `zleft tip`.
  fbtedge l tip, fbtedge x2 tip, zfbtedge l tip, zfbtedge x2 tip -- the same textured (TEX_RED, its texel at linear 0x100000, outside
    the frame 0x300000..0x395fff that the render clears): FB1t, FB2t, and FB3t (l tip) or FB4t (x2 tip); table 5 as `texedges2 l tip`,
    `texedges2 x2 tip`, `ztedges2 l tip`, `texzleft tip`.
  palcfg x2 tip (1,2) RED, frame 0, PALETTE_CFG 3, PALETTE[0] 0x10000 -- LEFT3R (LEFT3 raised 157 rows) row 2 spans -1..1: column 1;
    its rows -57..-1 return at `y < 0`.  Red: PC1t (`x > 3`), PC2t (`y < 3`), PC4t (`x1 < 0 && x2 < 3`), and PL1t, PL2t, PL4t (the
    same at 0x10000).  Table 5: as `texedges2 x2 tip` -- each LEFT3R row carries LEFT3's x values, and the y compares table 5 varies
    (`y < 1`, `y < zw`, `y >= ysize - 1`, `y >= ysize - 2 zw`) leave rows 2 and 69 drawn; except Nt, below.
  palcfg l tip (1,69) RED -- LREVM (LREV raised 190 rows) row 69 arrives 1 / -1 and is swapped: column 1.  Red: PC1t, PC3t (`x1 < 3 &&
    x2 < 0`), PL1t, PL2t, PL3t.  Table 5: as `texedges2 l tip`.
  zpalcfg x2 tip, zpalcfg l tip -- the Z-off twins: the same cells; table 5 as `texzleft tip` and `ztedges2 l tip`.
  NOT PREDICTED: Nt_inner_or on the four palcfg rows.  `x > 0 || x < d->xsize` draws LEFT3R's row 0 (-3..3) at ofs -3..-1:
    vram_z[-3..-1] is read (and written Z-on), and vram at fbofs -6..-1 (C's % keeps the sign) -- before both host allocations,
    undefined behaviour.  `texedges2`'s LEFT3 starts at row 100, where the same columns land on row 99.  (Y2t, row -1: NOT PREDICTED
    already.)

